6543	    /// fizzle arm protects is real, so the positive test is not vacuous. If a
6544	    /// fizzled turn does NOT undo its tentative pop (the pre-fix behavior), the
6545	    /// next pass's step2 removal drain calls `remove_tid` while
6546	    /// `tentative_selection` is `Some`, and the run queue's transaction guard
6547	    /// panics. This is precisely the panic `undo_tentative_pop` prevents.
6548	    #[test]
